{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "During a spring pilot with the incoming seventh-grade cohort, I found that the Pathways Grade 6 edition repeats material students have already mastered, while the Pathways Grade 7 edition matches the required seventh-grade sequence. I recorded these pilot results in my planning notes but have not yet sent them to the curriculum office. Given that the draft plan currently proposes the Grade 6 edition, I strongly recommend we switch to the Grade 7 edition before finalizing this adoption."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Mr. Grant. That's a significant finding — if the Grade 6 edition repeats material students have already mastered and the Grade 7 edition matches the required seventh-grade sequence, that's a strong case for switching editions. I'm noting this as a critical issue we'll need to address before finalizing. Now, Mr. Reed, please go ahead and share the HR compliance considerations regarding the proposed timeline, and then Ms. Haddad and Ms. Shah, we'll hear your respective concerns about language services and licensing as well. I want to make sure we have all implementation requirements on the table before I make any decisions."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I've reviewed the publisher's current license and confirmed that the district must provide one individually assigned digital account per student and one authorized print copy per student. The license permits 96 print copies for this cohort, which matches our expected enrollment of 96 students. However, the license does not permit shared classroom-code access, which is what the draft plan currently proposes. This means the draft plan's digital access model is non-compliant, and the proposed 80 printed copies fall short of the required one-per-student minimum. These licensing requirements will need to be corrected before the plan can be approved."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Thank you, Dr. Brooks. I'd like to share my language-service findings now. My enrollment review identified 14 students in the incoming seventh-grade cohort who require the Arabic version of the materials, in addition to students who use the Spanish version. I've confirmed with the publisher that both Spanish and Arabic editions are available for this resource, but the language-service request has not yet been added to the adoption plan. This means the current draft plan — which proposes English-only materials — does not meet the needs of all 96 students and will need to be updated to include the Spanish and Arabic editions before finalization."}
```

